- Is a very interesting time in
my life because just recently,

00:01:47.415 --> 00:01:50.222
on the beginning of the year
there was a part of me that was,

00:01:50.222 --> 00:01:53.631
everything that I do 
I have to be obsessed about.

00:01:53.631 --> 00:01:54.655
- All-in.

00:01:54.655 --> 00:01:56.780
- I think that you can be good
at many things, you can only be

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.767
great at the things
you're passionate about.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:01:59.682
- Yep.

00:01:59.682 --> 00:02:02.064
- I've been doing real
estate for about 10 years now.

00:02:02.064 --> 00:02:03.936
I'm part of the show 
"Million Dollar Listing" which

00:02:03.936 --> 00:02:07.238
just finished this 
season five and--

00:02:07.238 --> 00:02:08.682
- And you've been 
on since season two?

00:02:08.682 --> 00:02:09.597
- Season two, yes.

00:02:09.597 --> 00:02:11.013
- So you did four
seasons of the show.

00:02:11.013 --> 00:02:12.723
- Four seasons together.

00:02:12.723 --> 00:02:14.915
At the beginning of this year
there was something about me

00:02:14.915 --> 00:02:17.880
that was, I consider
myself to be a very happy guy.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.628
And when the year started I was,

00:02:19.628 --> 00:02:21.596
there was part of me that
was very, very sad.

00:02:21.596 --> 00:02:23.684
Normally, you're in a situation

00:02:23.684 --> 00:02:25.278
and you can identify 
why you're sad.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.358
You lose something, 
you miss something,

00:02:26.358 --> 00:02:27.963
your girlfriend leaves you, 
you're sad.

00:02:27.963 --> 00:02:31.115
At this particular moment I did
not know what I was sad about.

00:02:31.115 --> 00:02:33.488
I think I've been sad for quite
some time but I was very good at

00:02:33.488 --> 00:02:36.024
convincing myself that
things could be worked out.

00:02:36.024 --> 00:02:39.794
But at this point it just seems
to be the one time that I just

00:02:39.794 --> 00:02:40.850
couldn't convince myself.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.326
And has been eight days under
my sheets without waking up and

00:02:44.326 --> 00:02:45.942
that to me was very strange.

00:02:45.942 --> 00:02:50.062
The fact that I could not point
out exactly what the reason why

00:02:50.062 --> 00:02:54.562
was and one day I remember this
was the beginning of the year

00:02:54.562 --> 00:02:56.952
I came to

00:02:56.952 --> 00:03:00.152
I was shooting 
the next day on

00:03:00.152 --> 00:03:02.260
"Million Dollar Listing" where
you sit down in the interview

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.938
chair and you explain everything
that's going on in the scene and

00:03:03.938 --> 00:03:05.231
I called a friend of 
mine and I said,

00:03:05.231 --> 00:03:06.534
"Listen I don't 
want to shoot.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.680
"I'm very, very sad and the
fact I don't understand

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.763
"why am I sad 
makes me even sadder.

00:03:10.763 --> 00:03:13.627
"I just don't understand
because I want to fix it."

00:03:13.627 --> 00:03:15.717
At some point I started crying
and crying but like I've never

00:03:15.717 --> 00:03:17.643
cried in my life.

00:03:17.643 --> 00:03:19.735
When I had nothing left
I sort of saw something.

00:03:19.735 --> 00:03:24.073
I said you know when you're
hungry your stomach growls.

00:03:24.073 --> 00:03:25.866
So you feed it and it stops.

00:03:25.866 --> 00:03:28.825
I think the mind works
like that in some capacity.

00:03:28.825 --> 00:03:31.404
Where it's instead of growls

00:03:31.404 --> 00:03:34.004
or roars or whatever 
it becomes sad.

00:03:34.004 --> 00:03:35.535
We don't know we can feed it.

00:03:35.535 --> 00:03:36.988
There's something that was
missing and I was trying to

00:03:36.988 --> 00:03:38.517
understand what that was.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:41.746
At that point, when I already
sort of lost, I was about to open

00:03:41.746 --> 00:03:44.821
the door that I already knew
what was behind it but I didn't

00:03:44.821 --> 00:03:49.136
